  "content": {
    "_uid": "0804b161-c1b8-65b6-571e-09253e0f36fa",
    "body": [
      {
        "_uid": "77ea9442-34f7-9fbb-4d14-216f9f028ce1",
        "content": {
          "type": "doc",
          "content": [
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "\"Almost one-third of our life is spent sleeping, which is why a regular sleep routine is so important,\" said Dr Mughis Sheerani, Consultant Neurologist, AKUH. Though sleep is usually associated with inactivity, the brain maintains equal if not superior levels of electric activity during sleep time as compared with waking hours, and is extremely important for various functions of the body.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            },
            {
              "type": "paragraph",
              "content": [
                {
                  "text": "To highlight the issues surrounding sleep deprivation and disorders, AKUH will host a public awareness programme to commemorate World Sleep Day at the University's auditorium, with presentations by a number of physicians from different specialties.",
                  "type": "text"
                }
              ]
            }
          ]
        },
